label act1_day8:

    "Tuesday"

    scene bg bedroom
    "*VRRMMMM VRRRMMMM*" #[Phone Vibrate sound bit here]
    "I'm awakened by the muffled vibrations that are coming from the floor."

    "As I slowly reach for my phone to...not feel it on my nightstand. Great. I glance towards the floor to see my pants being the source of the sound."

    mc "How the hell did I forget to-"

    "Oh yeah. The poem. Took a bit more out of me than I thought it would."

    "I reach for my pants while still in the bed and pull out my phone to see."

    mc "7:18?! CRAP!!"
    "I hop out of bed and run to the bathroom to give myself a quick sink shower. I then throw on my clothes and pack my bag making sure I remember and head downstairs."

    scene bg house

    "As I make it outside I look down the road, I realize that Sayori is nowhere to be found."

    mc "Huh. I would have thought she would have come to check on me. Did she..."

    "I glance down the road to see if she left without me, but I don't spot any red bows in sight."

    "I pull out my phone and see that it's getting late. I know she typically wakes up late as well, but never THIS late. "

    "Should I just go on without her? Did she go on without me?"

    mc "Just call her, moron."

    "I tap her contact and begin to hit the call button. As I put the phone to my ear, I hear a loud slam."

    s "IM HERE! IM HERE!!!"

    "She runs over to me huffing and out of breath as I lower my phone and end the call."
    s "I MADE IT JUST IN TIME!"

    mc "Yup. Just in time. To make the BOTH of us late."

    "Sayori begins to pout as we begin to speedwalk to school."

    s "It's not my fault school is so far."

    "I begin to side eye her"

    mc "Sayori. It's a 15 minute walk."

    s "Well if it was 5, we wouldn't be in this predicament!"

    mc "You're right. Our parents should have bought a house even closer to the school instead of you making sure you wake up on time."

    "Sayori huffs at me while looking away."

    s "Don't have to be such a meanie about it.  "

    mc "Hey, I can't say much this time. I was only out here for a bit before trying to call you."

    s "See! I'm not the only one! Did you think your alarm was just in your dreams too?"

    "I glance at her with a raised eyebrow. What kind of dream..."

    mc "Uh..no. It was more muffled and I didn't hear it well. I forgot to plug it up last night."

    s "What were you doing last night to make you forget? I thought you already had all your homework caught up."

    mc "It was...the poem."

    s "OOOO! You were up all night working on it! Can I see can I see can I see!!!"

    mc "Hey woah now, miss 'Vice President'. Shouldn't we be waiting until club starts to share our poems?"

    s "Oh..heh heh..uh...yeah. But I am excited to see what you wrote. The others too!"

    scene bg residential_day

    "As I think about the others, I begin to wonder. "

    "My mind then lands on Monika. Her song lyrics were so somber. Will her poetry be the same or was her song just emotional for the sake of the song itself? "

    "I mean, song lyrics are poems in their own way. But the one she performed yesterday had a different tone."

    "Maybe I'm overthinking this. It's Monika. Of course she would be good at a variety of things. Just like Sayori said, she's great."

    s "Hellooo. Earth to [player]. You in there Space Ace?"

    "I come back to with Sayori waving her hand in my face."

    mc "Huh! Oh. Sorry. What were you saying?"

    s "Pfft...nevermind. What were you thinking about?"

    mc "Oh, Mon-"

    "I stop myself before I say Monika's name as Sayori perks up at me and gets a sly look on her face."

    s "Were you gonna say Monik-"

    mc "MONDAY'S THE SCHOOL  FESTIVAL RIGHT!!!"

    "Sayori jumps back a bit from my outburst."

    mc "I was uh, just thinking about what activities there would be and what not, you know."

    "Sayori begins to squints her eye at me."

    s "You spyin on me?"

    mc "What?! No! Why would I- Why would you...wait. Does this have to do with the fest-"

    s "OhLookHowQuickWeMadeItToSchoolGottaGoToClassOkayByeeeeee...."

    "She shuffles off into the crowd as we reach the front gates."

    " Oh, boy. I wonder what they're planning for us."

    scene bg club_day

    "As I walk into the clubroom, I see that I'm the last one to arrive. "

    "I see Yuri in her usual spot reading, Natsuki is just now coming out of the closet and making herself comfortable under the window on the floor with a manga and Sayori is talking to Monika."

    "As I walk in, they both notice me entering. While Monika gives a soft wave hello, Sayori is trying to avoid eye contact with me."

    mc "Hey guys. How are yo-"

    s "Busy with some important stuff."

    mc "Oh you mean the fe-"

    s "Featured activity of sharing poems! Yup! You got it. Why don't you go over there to get yourself ready, okay."

    "I glance at Monika as she face palms with a smile on her face."

    mc "Okay dear leaders. I'll leave you to...whatever you were doing..."

    "As I walk away I can faintly hear their conversation."

    m "I think you're right that he knows. Are you sure you didn't slip up anywhere about it?"

    s "My trap has been shut, locked, and key destroyed. I still think he's been spying on me..."
    "I mean, if I was, it would be fair game since she started the spy game in the first place."

    "As I sit on the other side of the room, I take my poem out and give it a quick read over. "

    "Geez. I really laid it on thick. I mean, I tried to make it more abstract but...I hope the others don't judge me too harshly."

    mc "*Sigh* I get it now..."

    m "Get what now?"

    "Monika's voice startles me a bit, causing me to slightly jump in my seat."

    m "Oh, sorry. I didn't mean to catch you off guard."

    mc "No, it's okay. I tend to space out a bit. I was just thinking about what Natsuki and Yuri meant about being nervous sharing and I'm starting to get it now."

    mc "It's the whole uncertainty of how others will receive it and...I guess I probably should have done something less for my first one."

    m "Yeah, nerves are a little tense right now."

    "I look up to Monika and see her glancing towards the others."

    " I follow suit and see Yuri scratching at her arm as she reads."

    " I look over to Natsuki and she is tapping away at the cover of her manga as Sayori approaches her and begins sitting next to her."

    "As I begin to look down again, Monika steps over to my side and places her hand on my back."

    m "Writing poetry can be very personal and sincere. I already know you and everyone else is worried about what critiques others will have."
    mc "Exactly. Which is why I should have written about something other tha-"

    "As I sit there silently, Monika speaks up again."

    m "Don't worry. We're all friends here. You don't need to feel ashamed of sharing anything personal here."

    mc "Heh..I wish I had your confidence."

    m "To be honest, I'm not always that confident. About a lot of things."

    mc "Really?"

    "Monika nods her head."

    m "There's quite a handful of things that I lose all nerves about. But as president, I have to set a good example for others to follow. Hopefully my confidence helps you find your own."

    "I look back at Monika and smile at her."

    mc "You know, I think it's working. Thank you."

    "Monika smiles back."

    m "Just doing my job! And speaking of which..."

    "Monika turns to the rest of the club with Sayori now sitting next to Yuri and talking to her."

    m "Okay, everyone!"

    m " It's the moment we've all been waiting for. Let's start sharing our poems with each other. "

    m "Now since we're at an odd number, we can have one person take time to reflect on their reception while the others wait. Do we have a volunteer for the first one to-"

    y "I CAN WAIT FIRST!!!"

    "Yuri's outburst catches us all a bit off guard, but unsurprised. She then begins to retreat back and hide behind her hair."

    y "I..if no one else has any objections."

    "We all glance at Natsuki as she looks back past us."

    n "Eh. I got no problem with it. Might as well get this over with."

    y "*Sigh* Thank you, you all for the added reprieve."

    "As we pair off, I begin to try to gravitate to Sayori as I feel she will understand it better. My attempt was met with an eager grin of the bow haired ball of sunshine."

    s "You! You! [player]! We shall share poems first!"

    mc "Yeah, I was actually hoping for this."

    s "Don't worry. I know it's your first time so I'll be gentle."

    mc "Uhh..."

    n "Geez, get a room Sayori."

    ##"Sayori's face goes from a look of confusion to awareness, and then to utter embarrassment."

    s "That is NOT how that was supposed to- ffffmmmm...."

    "I begin to chuckle at the situation she got herself into as we walk over to the other side of the classroom."

    mc "Well, here you go."

    s "Thank you, sir! And here you are as well."
    ###Sayori poem

    "As I read the poem I can't help to revel in both the quality and personality of her poem. "

    "While I can see the happiness in the words, there's a bit of a somber tone over them. And that last line..."

    "Wait..."

    mc "We're you late because you were writing your poem this morning?"

    "Sayori gulps."

    s "Whaa? Nahhh. What makes ya say that..."

    "Mc: I could be wrong, but it's quite odd to be craving breakfast late at night."

    s "Sounds like someone's never had pancakes for dinner."

    mc "Wait a minute..."

    "I hold her paper up to my nose and sniff it."

    mc "Sayori I can smell the syrup."

    s "MmmmFine! But I just finished it this morning. I kinda had a bit of a block last night. Besides, you were late too."

    mc "But still earlier than you. I even finished my poem last night like I was supposed to."
    s "Stop being a meanie and get back to the poem. Did you understand it?"

    mc "Oh, umm. I think? What I got from it was...uh, hope for the future, but there's still that bit of fear of something bad happening. "

    mc "Kinda like a leap of faith? Kinda...bittersweet, but more sweet than bitter."

    s "That's pretty much it? Yeah, bittersweet poems are kinda my thing."

    mc "I'm kind of surprised you like writing about sad things."

    s "Well, it's kinda flat to be gung-ho about just happy things. Without reflecting on the sad stuff, it's harder to appreciate the happy moments."

    "I guess I never realized how much depth Sayori really has even after all this time. But is that because we grew apart or because I never saw it in the first place?"

    mc "Well, good job. Very well done. So, what did you think of mine?"

    s "Huh?! Oh! I uhhh..was too focused on your reaction to mine I forgot to read it."

    "She clonks on her head as she sticks out her tongue before she begins to read my poem."

    "I can see her face slowly fade from anticipation to a somber concern."

    s "Is this about...you know.... Elsea?"

    mc "I mean, kinda. Mainly about how I've been feeling lately."

    "Sayori sets my poem on the nearby desk and grabs my hand with a soft smile."

    s "You know, I'm always here for you."

    "I smile back at her."
    mc "Yeah. I know. I've actually been feeling better since Sunday. It's just that nothing felt right while writing. Then I started to think about Monika's poem and..."

    "Sayori lets go of my hand and sets back a bit."

    s "O oh.Y-yeah. Uhh."

    "She shakes her head a bit and smiles."

    s "I'm glad! I told you she was great. Glad to see you finally coming around."

    mc "Uh. Yeah. I guess I am. So, what were your thoughts?"

    s "Honestly? Pretty great. Sure, a bit bleak, but the emotion is there and gets the message across quite well."

    mc "Huh. Thanks. I was worried it would be too bland. I was a bit scared to dig deep."

    s "And it paid off. Now that I know you have the potential, I can't wait to read the next [player] original."

    mc "Don't get your hopes up. This was probably my peak."

    s "Nope! My hopes are staying sky high cus you'll only get better with practice!"

    mc "Heh. Thanks. That means a lot."

    "As we switch off to our next member, I head off to Natsuki, who is staring daggers at her poem."

    "I stand in front of her quietly as she sharply looks up. "

    mc "You...doin..fine?"

    "Natsuki then looks down and away from me."
    n "Eh..."

    mc "Y-yeah. I kinda feel that too. I guess you were right about the whole awkwardness thing."

    n "You say that like I'm ever wrong. Whatever. Just...Here!"

    "She flings her poem towards me and holds it out for me to take."

    ###Natsuki's poem

    "As I read her poem, its style is surprising. "

    "For someone so rough around the edges, this poem is quite sweet and bouncy. I wouldn't dare tell her to her face, but this style is quite 'cute'."

    " And the ending. It felt like someone jumping on a pogo stick and falling flat on their face on purpose for a comedic effect."

    "As I look up from the poem to her, I open my mouth and-"

    n "I figured you wouldn't like it."

    mc "Huh?"

    n "I can see it in your face. That little eyebrow crap you do?"

    mc "Eyebrow crap? Wait, I do that? What are you-"

    n "*Groan* Just come out and say you hate it so we can get it over with."

    mc "Fine. I like it."

    n "See! I told you, you-"

    n "...Huh?"

    mc "I like it."

    "Natsuki begins to squint her eyes at me."

    n "What part exactly?"

    mc "I have to break that down to you?"

    n "If you don't then you're either a liar or you're a moron. To be honest, the latter does make sense..."

    mc "Okay, Fine! I like that the poem is simple, yet strong. To me, it means the best we can do is try because that's what we're made to do."

    mc "I like how it starts with such a rhythmic bounce to it and then falls flat at the end to subvert expectations."

    "Natsuki stands there staring kinda stunned."

    n "You're not just saying that to try and be nice are you?"

    mc "I'd say my only complaint was that it's too short, but I feel you would take that personally."

    "Natsuki then smiles as she jabs me in the arm."

    n "You jerk. Well, at least you're not a liar. And I guess  I can take moron off the table as well since you have enough sense to recognize a pro."

    mc "Why thank you oh great pro."

    "Natsuki chuckles to herself with a big grin on her face."

    mc "So, do you mind giving my poem a read?"

    n "Sure, I'd be happy to give you some pointers."

    "As I hold my poem out to her, she almost snatches it out of my hands. I can't tell if it was out of eagerness or pure aggression. With her, it's quite a toss up."

    "As she reads it the slight smug look on her face slowly turns into one of concern. As she hands it back to me, she rubs the back of her head."

    n "Uh. It doesn't suck so, good job."

    mc "Thanks? So, that's it?"

    n "That depends. Are you...okay? That was kind of a downer."

    mc "Yeah. Just had some stuff to get off my chest and I read something that kinda inspired it out of me."

    n "Well, that makes sense. Especially for your first poem. It's good for what it is. Not great, but not crap."

    mc "Wow. Mediocrity. Such high praise from the pro of poetry. Thank you Miss Poetry."

    n "Tee hee. That's actually a good one. See. Simple stuff like that can be powerful. You don't need fancy words to write."

    mc "Mmhhmm. Few words work well."

    "Natsuki starts glaring at me."

    n "Look. If I need a dictionary and 4 lines for me to understand that you said ' I walked down the street', then you failed your job as a poet."

    mc "Huh. I never thought of it that way. I'm gonna keep that in mind. Thanks."

    n "No problem."

    "Natsuki hands me my poem as she walks over to Sayori. I take a look at who to go to next as Monika walks up to me."

    m "So, how are you doing so far?"

    mc "Oh. I'm fine. I guess I'm not as bad as I thought I'd be."

    m "Oh? Sounds like you found a talent."

    mc "Well, I wouldn't take it that far."

    m "So, are you wanting to sit this one out or wait a bit more."

    mc "If you don't mind, I would like to get to see everyone's first. I can sit out last"

    m "Ah. Looking to reflect on everyone's input?"

    mc "Yeah. See the differences and the notes before I start thinking about it more. "

    mc "Sayori and Natsuki showed me a few things and they're clicking. I wanna see if you and Yuri have similar outlooks."

    m "We I'm glad to hear about the initiative! Tell you what, I can sit it out and you can go on to Yuri. I'm sure she'll give you quite a bit to reflect on."

    mc "Yeah. Sounds good."

    "Monika smiles and walks back to her desk."

    " I turn to Yuri who is reading her poem to herself. I wonder how she'll react to my poem. Hell, the way she reads, she might blow through it in 5 seconds flat."

    "As I walk up to her she notices me instantly."

    y "Why hello, [player]. How has the activity treated you so far?"

    mc "Good. I do get what you and Natsuki were talking about with the nerves though, but it's getting a bit better."

    "Yuri begins to smile nervously."

    y "Ahh..yes. Uh..I will admit that the prospect made me apprehensive, the session with Monika was quite enjoyable and really calmed my initial anxieties. "

    y "Although the vulnerability of sharing brings with it the possibility of being ridiculed or not taken seriously, the euphoria of not only experiencing someone else's emotional expressions, and watching them unfurl my poetic tapestry in real time is just-"

    "Yuri stops in her tracks and stares at me like a deer in headlights and begins to hide behind her hair."

    y "Sorry. I didn't mean to ramble."

    "I smile gently at her."

    mc "Hey. Don't worry about it. I'm glad that you're enjoying yourself. I'm just hoping I don't disappoint. No question, your poem is gonna make mine look like child's play."

    "As Yuri is giving me a sympathetic look, she takes a deep breath and composes herself."

    y "There is no need to underestimate your own abilities by comparing your work to my own. "

    y "I have had many years of experience with both producing and engaging with the medium, so a greater expectation is understandable. "

    y "As this is your introductory attempt, it is expected to have the tells of an amateur. As you hone your skills, these early endeavors will be great milestones to look back on."

    mc "Huh. Is that so?"
    y "Indeed. When I think about my first few poems, well, now they seem quite..."

    mc "Cringe?"

    "Yuri is caught a bit off guard by my input. As she thinks about it, she slowly nods her head."

    mc "Well in that case, I can read yours first. Maybe seeing your style will spark something in mine."

    "Yuri's eyes begin to gleam with delight"

    y "It would be a great honor to become a mentor for your literary endeavors!"

    "She excitedly hands me her poem. I grab it with a smile, that slowly turns into a frustrated facade."
    ###Yuri Poem
    "What the hell did I just read? "

    "What the hell is a tendril? "

    "Why is there only one street lamp left in the world it seems? "

    "Do the colors actually mean something? "

    "And where the hell is the ghost? "

    "Is she the ghost? "

    "Are the lights ghosts? "

    "This feels like I just sat down to start an anime and the first episode I see is half way through the series."

    "I begin to hear a strange sound coming from in front of me. As I look up, I see the source of the noise is a distressed looking Yuri making a high pitched moan."
    mc "Uhh...the words are uh..written quite well!"

    "My response seems to have granted Yuri some relief as she lets out a sigh."

    y "I am glad that my message was not lost in your reading. I was hoping the decreased length would assist others in the intended comprehension, although I do prefer longer forms to dive more into the complexities of such subjects."

    "...What?"

    "Wait..."

    mc "S-sorry. To be honest, this really flew waaaay over my head. What I mean was that the uh..handwriting...was..pretty..."

    "The shock and embarrassment is shown on Yuri's face."

    y "I-I didn't mean to..uhh..."

    "She begins to hide her face in her hair as we sit in silence for a while.[I want to see if my rewrite of this part of the line works better. Show the sprite that shows her embarrassed behind her hair.] "

    "We sit in silence for a moment."

    "Great job, dummy. You broke her."

    "She doesn't seem like she's going to recover on her own so I decide to try and break the awkwardness."

    mc "Yuri? It's alright. This just means I got a lot to learn."

    y "I just feel...too..."

    "I place my hand on her shoulder and she jumps a bit."

    mc "Think of it this way; You just gave me not only the goal to improve my writing, but to improve my reading. "

    mc "Plus, what you've got is something I will want to read over and over again and it will be different each time."

    y "That...is an inherent accomplishment goal for me..."

    mc "Well then, mission accomplished!"

    "Yuri cracks a smile behind her hair."

    y "Th-thank you [player]. For your kindness."

    mc "Hey, it's no issue. If you don't mind, can you elaborate on what it meant?"

    "As Yuri pushes her hair from her face, she regains her composure and accepts her poem back from me. "

    "She takes a deep breath and begins to close her eyes to regain her composure."

    y "Everyone has a habit ingrained in their being, be it nature or nurture, a hobby or a routine. "

    y "While this is a universal reality for us, said habit may be unique in one way or another. "

    y "The qualities that make these habits unique can also become quite uncomfortable to display to peers, let alone strangers. "

    y "That was my muse during this writing session."

    mc "I think I can see that now. I actually can relate with my random zone outs. "

    mc "I have had those awkward snap backs to reality. "

    mc "Well, thanks for the insight!"

    y "You are welcome. If you do not mind, might I read your poem?"

    mc "Oh, yeah. I almost forgot."

    "As I pull out mine to hand to her I can't help but feel inadequate. "

    "The poem she wrote was more complex than I was expecting. I hope mine isn't too boring for her. "

    "As I watch her reaction, I can't help be realize how long its taking her to read it. "

    "Was my handwriting that sloppy? I mean, I know I'm not that neat, but I figured I was at least legible. "

    "As I take a deep breath out of suspense, I catch Yuri's attention."

    y "Oh! I-I'm sorry. I got lost in analyzing!"

    mc "No, no. It's okay. I'm just glad you can read my writing. I'll actually take that as a good sign then."

    y "Is it acceptable for me to query you for a moment?"

    mc "Uh..Sure. Go ahead."

    y "I do not mean to pry into your personal matters, but I am picking up a personal loss that can be seen as significant. And it is your struggle to deal with such a loss."

    "Hit the nail on the head with that one."

    mc "Y-yeah. Exactly. I have been dealing with some issues and I...I guess this helped me conceptualize them."
    y "Are you doing alright? I know that Sayori is already a source of comfort, but if you need another outlet with fewer historical ties, I have no issues lending an ear."

    mc "Thanks for that. I am doing better. I'm just still working through it."

    "Yuri smiles at me and returns back to my poem."

    mc "So, what's the verdict?"

    y "While there are a few troupes that are quite cliche such as the mirror and rain metaphors and the a b rhyme scheme, they are common for most first time poets and are implemented here quite adequately."

    y "I would say that this is a solid beginning to what could be an accomplished writer."

    mc "Woah. You mean, it wasn't bad at all?"

    "Yuri shakes her head with a light smile."

    y "It was a good attempt for someone who claims to have no experience. Well done!"

    mc "Thanks! And I will try to keep that in mind about those troupes. Do you have any suggestions?"

    "Yuri's face beams with delight at the prospect of sharing more of her interest."

    y "I can- no wait there is...oooh what about-"

    m "Okay guys, time to switch it up!"

    "We both turn to Monika standing next to us as Sayori is waving Yuri towards her."

    mc "If you want, make sure to write down your recommendations and give them to me later."

    y "Certainly! I will make sure to only select the best!"

    "As she hands me back my poem, she walks over to Sayori."

    m "Well, looks like you're on your last partner. How's it been? Sounds like you're getting some good feedback."

    mc "I'll admit, I was quite nervous. But seeing how different everyone's style is puts things in perspective."

    m "Glad to hear the reception has been positive for you! "

    m "See, even though we have our own biases to our own styles, we can still appreciate the differences in each other and grow as a collective."

    mc "Yeah. I feel like I learn a lot more from everyone through this than I thought. And I got to save the best for last."

    "..."

    "Did I just say that?"

    "Monika is staring at me with her face turning red. "

    "Oh no..."

    mc "Not that I'm saying you're better than the others! And not worse either! You're all just different and you're a good different. A great different! And-"

    "My rambling is cut short by Monika's chuckle to herself."

    m "Well, thank you for such a high regard. The top of your list is a great place to be. I don't mind sharing the spot with the others."

    mc "Umm. Yeah. Um thanks for understanding."

    m "Anytime. So, let's see what you have for us. I've been waiting to see this."

    mc "Okay. I hope you don't-"

    m "Stop selling yourself short all the time. Even if you don't think it's the best, it was still your best."

    "All the other girls have been so supportive. The worst review I got was a meh. Of course Monika would take it positively."

    mc "I'm sorry. You're right. I hope you enjoy it."

    "Her bright smile lights up the room as she takes my poem."

    "That brightness soon fades as she begins reading and is eclipsed with a look of concern. As she looks up to me, I brace myself for the inevitable question."

    m "I'm glad you're able to express yourself in a healthy way."

    "That...was not a question."

    m "I respect your boundaries so I won't pry. But I want you to know that not only I, but we are here for you. I wish you all the best as you get through your hardships."

    "She...didn't ask? Not even infer."

    " She has to know about it, yeah. She does. And that's why she's not asking about it. She actually...wow."

    mc "Th-thanks. I am getting better, but thanks for that."

    m "As for your poem as a whole, how should I put this...are you sure this is your first time writing?"

    mc "Yeah..."

    m "Well color me surprised! This is quite good! There's a few things that can be improved for sure, but I wouldn't say it's bad in the least. Keep this up, and you might be able to teach me a thing or two."

    "I'm completely shocked by the positivity. Am I actually kinda good at this?"

    mc "You, you're just saying that, right?"

    "Monika looks at me with a bit of disappointment as she sighs."

    m "Okay, fine. The pacing is stumbling throughout. There could have been better word choices. "

    m "The rhyme attempt is very basic. Also, the metaphor of the mirror as a source of introspection is quite shallow."

    mc "Oh. Umm. I see..."

    m "Still, with all those technical faults, it's the execution and the imagery that make it good. "

    m "Just by reading this, you are showing others a deep part of you. That alone takes skill, not to mention courage."

    "I sit in silence as I reflect on her words. I don't believe she's just trying to make me feel better. I truly believe she likes it for what it is. All of them did."

    mc "Thanks. I think I needed both the good and the bad to put things in perspective. Rather know what I'm doing wrong so it doesn't stay bad for too long... I kinda had to learn that the hard wa-"

    "Oh crap! Why did I bring that up like that? Monika starts looking down to avoid eye contact."

    mc "A-anywho, uh, mind if I read your poem now?"
    m "Oh, yes. Certainly."

    "Uhhh..huh..."

    "So Monika and Yuri are gonna give my brain a run for my money here. Man, I have no idea what's going on."

    " Well, based on Yuri's poem, it's probably an abstract concept."

